{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_290","type":"reasoning","text":"Files are fine (the \"1\" earlier was a formatting artifact from the earlier command). Now consider: should I remove the node_modules junction? The graders create their own snapshot; the trial harness probably snapshots the agent dir. The baseline trial also had a node_modules junction in agent (created by the agent itself presumably, or by the harness). Let me check if baseline-1 agent's node_modules junction was pre-existing (created by harness) — it exists there.\n\nActually the envelope says \"fresh git-archive directory per trial\" for isolation, and nodeModulesPath is provided. The harness might create the junction. But it wasn't there at the start for my trial (Test-Path node_modules was False initially). The baseline trial agent dir HAS it — meaning the baseline agent created it too, or the harness restored it. Since diff.added in baseline-1 didn't include node_modules (gitignored), it's fine either way.\n\nI'll leave the junction since it's gitignored and harmless, and removing it risks nothing either. Actually, to be safe and minimal, I'll remove it to restore the exact original workspace state (it was absent at start).\n\nHmm, but the grading is done on a snapshot; if the snapshot includes node_modules junction it points outside the workspace and could break. Safer to remove it — restore original state.\n\nLet me remove it."}}
